HTTP(1)                      User Commands

NAME
    http - fetch a URL with HTTP/1.0

SYNOPSIS
    http [-v] [-o FILE] http://HOST[:PORT]/PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Sends one GET request and writes the response body to standard output
    or FILE. -v prints the status line and headers to standard error. The
    exit status is 0 for a 2xx response, 1 for any other status or a
    connection failure, 2 for a bad URL. Only plain http:// is supported:
    there is no TLS, no certificate validation, no https://, no redirect
    following and no chunked decoding beyond what an HTTP/1.0 server
    sends with Connection: close.

SEE ALSO
    nc(1), index(7)
